<article class="help-article p-4">
    <header class="help-article-header mb-4">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined help-article-icon">data_object</span>
        <h1 class="help-article-title">SQL Schema Viewer</h1>
        <p class="help-article-lead">
            The SQL Schema Viewer shows the database schema derived from your model and can export it
            as a MariaDB-compatible SQL file.
        </p>
    </header>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Open the viewer</h2>
    <p>
        In the Editor, choose <em>Show SQL Schema...</em> from the main menu. This action is available
        when the project supports SQL output.
    </p>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Review and export</h2>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li>Use zoom controls to zoom in, zoom out, reset zoom, or center the schema view.</li>
        <li>Choose <em>Export Schema</em> to save a SQL file to a selected folder.</li>
        <li>Enable <strong>Include sample data</strong> or <strong>Include comments</strong> before exporting.</li>
        <li>The exported schema targets MariaDB and is compatible with MySQL 5.7+ and MariaDB 10.2+.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="help-callout">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined">database</span>
        <div>
            <strong>Use the viewer as a sanity check.</strong>
            Review tables, columns, and relationships before relying on the generated schema downstream.
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
